title: Analytics › Payer by case mix
route: /analytics
intro: A grid with payers down and a kind of case across. Each cell is how often that payer approves that kind of case as requested, with how many decisions stand behind it. Four tabs change the columns. A cell opens its cases; a payer name opens the payer analysis.
dir: TD
also: A cell with fewer than 10 decisions is drawn grey with a dashed edge and the word 'few', so a small number is not read as a pattern. Color is never the only signal: a cell under 55% is striped with a down mark, a cell from 80% has an up mark, and every rate is printed.
---
start s1 "Scroll to 'Payer by case mix'"
screen sc "Tabs: 'Diagnosis group', 'Program', 'Request type', 'Population'\nColumns for diagnosis group: Alcohol use disorder, Opioid use disorder, Stimulant or other substance use, Depression or anxiety, Trauma-related, Co-occurring, 'All cases'\nA row for each payer and 'All payers'\nLegend: the color scale, 'Below 55%, striped', '80% and above', 'Fewer than 10 decisions'"
click t1 "Click a tab"
process t2 "The columns change: program (Residential 3.5, IOP, PHP, Detox), request type (Initial, Concurrent review, Reauthorization, Modification, Retrospective) or population (Adolescent, Adult, Dual-eligible, Pregnant or postpartum, First-time treatment, Prior admissions)"

group gHover "Hover or Tab to a cell"
  input h1 "Move over a cell or Tab to it"
  overlay h2 "Tooltip: payer and column, '53% approved as requested', '131 decisions', approved and not approved counts"
endgroup

click c1 "Click a cell (or press Enter on it)\nFor example Cardinal and Opioid use disorder, 53% of 131"
process p1 "Opens the case list panel with exactly those 131 cases\nAnd their reasons"
goto g1 "Continues in: Analytics › Case list panel"
click c2 "Click a payer name"
process p2 "Opens the payer analysis panel"
goto g2 "Continues in: Analytics › Payer analysis panel"
click c3 "Click a column heading"
process p3 "Opens the case list for that column across all payers"
click d1 "Click 'View data table'"
screen d2 "A table of rate and decisions for every cell"
process p4 "In the default view Cardinal's weakest cells are opioid use disorder and co-occurring, concurrent reviews and, in the case list, thin continued-stay evidence"

s1 --> sc --> t1 --> t2
sc --> h1 --> h2
sc --> c1 --> p1 --> g1
sc --> c2 --> p2 --> g2
sc --> c3 --> p3 --> g1
sc --> d1 --> d2
p1 -.-> p4
